    `Father, I receive today the portrait of Ruth — the woman who chose hesed when she had no obligation to, who clung when every circumstance argued for release, who went to a foreign people and a foreign land and brought nothing with her except the character that turned out to be the only thing that mattered. Let her story speak to me today about the kind of faithfulness that is available to me regardless of what I have lost and regardless of what I do not have. Where I have been waiting for better circumstances before I live with the kind of integrity Ruth demonstrated in the worst of hers, correct me. The strength and dignity of Proverbs 31:25 is not the product of good circumstances. It is the product of good character — and good character is available now, today, in this season, in this specific situation, with what I currently have. Let me be someone whose hesed toward others reflects Your hesed toward me.`
